 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 533149,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Find the lengths of the missing sides in the given figure.<br>\n<figure>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/f43a603496ec0b54.png\" alt=\"A right triangle with its legs marked b and 15. The hypotenuse is marked c. The angles at the bottom-left and bottom-right are labeled 90 degrees and 60 degrees.\">\n</figure>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "The side lengths are <span data-math=\"15,15\\sqrt 3,30.\">15,15\\sqrt 3,30</span>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The set of ratios in a 30°-60°-90° triangle are <span data-math=\"1:\\sqrt 3 :2\"></span>, or <span data-math=\"x:x\\sqrt 3 :2x\"></span>.</p>\n<p>Since you are shown the right angle and the 60° angle, you know the unmarked angle is a 30° angle.</p>\n<p>The side opposite the 30° angle is the shortest side, <span data-math=\"a = x = {\\text{ }}15\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"2x = {\\text{ }}2\\left( {15} \\right){\\text{ }} = {\\text{ }}30\"></span></p>\n<p><span data-math=\"x\\sqrt 3 = 15\\sqrt 3 \"></span></p>\n<p>The side lengths are 15, 30, <span data-math=\"15\\sqrt 3 \"></span>.</p>\n"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
